  "body": "Part of #3663 (the tool library dialog). Step U11: the Recipes tab. After U8 (the dialog frame).\n\n## What happens\n\n![recipes: mockup left, current right](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/toollib-compare/3-recipes.png)\n\nThe table of cutting data is there. There is no explanation, no mark on the material of the document, no derived values and no buttons to add or copy recipes.\n\n## Expected (mockup)\n\n- One line that says what a recipe is and when an operation uses it.\n- The table: material, rpm, feed, stepdown and the other columns, with a **★** on the row of the document's stock material.\n- Under each row, or for the selected row: the **derived** surface speed and chip load (read-only).\n- Buttons: **Add material**, **Suggest**, **Copy recipes from tool…**, and a note with the units.\n- Edits are undoable commands.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests: the ★ follows the document material; the derived values change with rpm and feed; Add, Suggest and Copy each land as one undo step.\n- The page layout test asserts the explanation, the columns and the buttons.\n- Before and after screenshots in the PR body.\n\nEffort: medium (one tab and its tests).\n",
